      "content": "that's a fair point. so it feels like a lot of these arguments are basically just ways to avoid fixing the problem. like, if the \"difficulty\" is just about paperwork or how to frame it, does that mean the opposition is fundamentally just about maintaining the status quo rather than having a valid legal or moral reason to say no?",
